+## Main execution document and required context
+
+**This file is the main implementation plan and execution guide.** It governs the redesign's scope, Phase 0–16 sequence and dependencies, screen/file mapping, acceptance gates, verification, cleanup, rollback and completion reporting. Use this file to select and track the authorized phase; do not execute from a supporting document alone.
+
+**Primary UI reference: [the Magic Patterns project](https://www.magicpatterns.com/c/jhv4ekfl4cidsa3phgrb3f).** Use its verified screens, components, states, interactions, animations and transitions as the design target throughout execution and visual acceptance. The Markdown documents, design breakdown and saved captures explain and document that reference; they do not replace it or authorize an independently interpreted redesign. Existing Android screens provide the behavior baseline, not the target appearance.
+
+For each authorized phase, inspect the corresponding reference screens/states and motion in Brave, compare them with the current Android implementation, and validate the result against the same reference. Recheck the displayed version/artifact: the inspected baseline is v32. If the project has changed, record the difference and reconcile the intended baseline before adopting it; do not silently expand scope. If reference access or a required state is unavailable, use the linked versioned evidence only within its stated limits and leave the unsupported fidelity claim unverified.
+
+For a visual discrepancy between a written summary and the verified reference, resolve it against the rendered reference and matching-version source, then update the documents together. Keep current functionality, settings, accessibility and frontend-only boundaries binding; document any necessary adaptation rather than copying prototype fixtures, unsupported actions or incidental defects.
+
+The following two documents are **required context to read and analyze**, not optional background:
+
+| Required context | How it informs execution |
+|---|---|
+| [Motion and fidelity specification](Resident_Android_MagicPatterns_Motion_and_Fidelity_Specification.md) | Apply the relevant M01–M16 animation definitions, source values, native adaptations, phase work packets, reduced-motion rules and visual/performance acceptance criteria. |
+| [Prototype inspection record](Resident_Android_MagicPatterns_Prototype_Inspection_Record.md) | Understand what was actually inspected, the evidence's confidence and limitations, observed prototype issues, unresolved states and remaining native/integration checks. Follow its linked capture evidence where relevant. |
+
+Before each authorized phase, read this main plan and both required context documents, analyze the relevant sections together, then inspect the current application code and reference evidence for that phase. Record which requirements/evidence apply, which adaptations are necessary and which checks remain unverified. Follow applicable user and `AGENTS.md` instructions throughout.
+
+The supporting documents supplement this main plan; they do not independently authorize work, expand scope, change phase order or convert unverified observations into completed checks. Reconcile any material inconsistency against the inspected evidence and current instructions, and synchronize the affected documents before relying on it. Do not silently discard evidence or weaken an acceptance gate. Keep phase progress and acceptance results in this main plan, motion-definition changes in the specification, and inspection findings/status in the record.
+
+This document hierarchy does not begin implementation. When a phase is authorized, execute only that phase and its permitted work, complete its acceptance checks, update the relevant documents and stop before the next phase unless the user authorizes continuation.
+
 ## Mandatory fidelity requirement
 
 **“Copy the same exact screens and smooth animations from Magic Patterns to resident Android.”** The authoritative reference is [this Magic Patterns design](https://www.magicpatterns.com/c/jhv4ekfl4cidsa3phgrb3f), v32 as rechecked in Brave for the fresh capture session. This is a reproduction task, not discretionary visual redesign or an invitation to approximate the layout with generic components.
